; A holding sold at a gain, written the way beancount writes one.
;
; `-10 HOOL {500.00 USD} @ 550.00 USD` says two different things: the basket
; is what the units cost, and the price is what they fetched. Beancount
; balances the entry at `units × cost` — the basket — and treats the price as
; information. The gain is the third posting, stated outright.
;
; Read the other way round, the holding was valued at 5,500.00 instead of the
; 5,000.00 it cost, the splits summed to the 500.00 gain, and GnuCash scrubbed
; in `Imbalance-USD 500.00` while the run reported one transaction and no
; error — the failure the empty-basket refusal and the unreadable-line refusal
; were both written to stop, arriving through the door those two closed.
;
; What this fixture produces: the holding at 5,000.00 USD of value, the cash
; at 5,500.00, the gain at -500.00, and no Imbalance.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
